(6454298, 957256, 112972, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by DrAchoo:</b></div><hr/><i> Great shot!  Going to be there in August.  Excited!!! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>That is great, Doc!  I''m sure you will love it.  My stay here has been much longer that I thought it would be mainly because I can''t get over the beauty in this area.  IMHO, Grant Teton blows Yellowstone out of the water by a mile.  Of course, it''s not really fair to compare the two.  YS is known for its geysers and hydrothermal activities while GT for its breathtaking mountains and sceneries.</td>', 'Originally posted by DrAchoo: Great shot!  Going to be there in August.  Excited!!!   That is great, Doc!  I''m sure you will love it.  My stay here has been much longer that I thought it would be mainly because I can''t get over the beauty in this area.  IMHO, Grant Teton blows Yellowstone out of the water by a mile.  Of course, it''s not really fair to compare the two.  YS is known for its geysers and hydrothermal activities while GT for its breathtaking mountains and sceneries.', '2011-06-27 18:17:15.000000', NULL, 0),
