(6455714, 957469, 72929, '<td valign="top">@littlemav:<br/> <br/>Yes, the stars ARE different colors. Color relates to size, surface temperature and the age of a star. In the brightest of stars, you can see with your eyes they are different colors. In the winter (northern hemisphere), Betelgeuse in Orion is red. Sirius, next to Orion is blue (for example). In the summer, there is Arcturus (red) and Vega (blue). You can see Arcturus as the brightest star just past overhead at sunset this month (In US / Europe / Japan).</td>', '@littlemav: Yes, the stars ARE different colors. Color relates to size, surface temperature and the age of a star. In the brightest of stars, you can see with your eyes they are different colors. In the winter (northern hemisphere), Betelgeuse in Orion is red. Sirius, next to Orion is blue (for example). In the summer, there is Arcturus (red) and Vega (blue). You can see Arcturus as the brightest star just past overhead at sunset this month (In US / Europe / Japan).', '2011-06-29 09:45:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(6455771, 957256, 74562, '<td valign="top">This is a big Wow, love that photo, Congratulations on your Blue</td>', 'This is a big Wow, love that photo, Congratulations on your Blue', '2011-06-29 11:49:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(6455794, 957462, 60862, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mgarsteck:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by levyj413:</b></div><hr/><i> Congrats on the shot, ribbon, personal best (and first time over 7.0.  Well deserved.<br/> <br/>I''m sorry to see, however, that it wasn''t enough for you: "Well Im glad I got a ribbon, but I was expecting something more than a yellow." </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Im happy and content to get the ribbon I just expected more out of the picture thats all.  Nothing wrong with wanting to go for the top right? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Of course!  Wanting to go for the top is natural.  Maybe you meant "expecting" as "hoping." I just get tired of others on DPC who indicate via their comments that they feel they''re entitled to the highest honors, as if the voters erred in choosing another shot to get a better score.</td>', 'Originally posted by mgarsteck: Originally posted by levyj413: Congrats on the shot, ribbon, personal best (and first time over 7.0.  Well deserved. I''m sorry to see, however, that it wasn''t enough for you: "Well Im glad I got a ribbon, but I was expecting something more than a yellow."   Im happy and content to get the ribbon I just expected more out of the picture thats all.  Nothing wrong with wanting to go for the top right?  Of course!  Wanting to go for the top is natural.  Maybe you meant "expecting" as "hoping." I just get tired of others on DPC who indicate via their comments that they feel they''re entitled to the highest honors, as if the voters erred in choosing another shot to get a better score.', '2011-06-29 12:27:47.000000', NULL, 0),
