(6456193, 957262, 46700, '<td valign="top">When I saw this, I thought it looked familiar.  I was in Estes park in 2007 for a wedding I shot and took this <a href="//www.nvphoto.com/Landscapes/Nature-Favorites/6209537_rLFZE#391479044_Y74qZ-A-LB" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">photo</a> <br/> <br/>Definitely taken from the same little bridge w/ a polarizer stacked w/ a Gradiant ND.  <br/> <br/>Nice work.  Not much has changed. <br/> <br/>Justin <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-06-29 21:07:11.</i></td>', 'When I saw this, I thought it looked familiar.  I was in Estes park in 2007 for a wedding I shot and took this photo  Definitely taken from the same little bridge w/ a polarizer stacked w/ a Gradiant ND.   Nice work.  Not much has changed.  Justin ', '2011-06-29 22:06:45.000000', '2011-06-29 22:07:11.000000', 0),
(6456201, 957462, 30982, '<td valign="top">Sorry you''re disappointed with the ribbon color.  I''ll take it off your hands if you don''t want it.  :-)  Still can''t get over the length of the exposure, and the sleeping birds!</td>', 'Sorry you''re disappointed with the ribbon color.  I''ll take it off your hands if you don''t want it.  :-)  Still can''t get over the length of the exposure, and the sleeping birds!', '2011-06-29 22:11:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(6456473, 957447, 91944, '<td valign="top">this is stunning would of giving it a ten if i voted. the house could have been left out in my opinion.</td>', 'this is stunning would of giving it a ten if i voted. the house could have been left out in my opinion.', '2011-06-30 08:21:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(6456477, 957447, 91944, '<td valign="top">how do you all find such beautiful places.</td>', 'how do you all find such beautiful places.', '2011-06-30 08:22:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(6456745, 957462, 90098, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ccarter:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice shot deserving of the award - but expected more then a yellow? A bit arrogant I''d say. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Like Levt said, hoping is a better word.  If you dont shoot for the best and have high expectations for your work then your work will not <br/>improve as quickly.  I want to be the best and so I shoot like it, and that mentality has done me well in my professional career.<br/> <br/>This is literally my favorite picture that I have taken so far, I only want the best for it, I take a lot of pride in them, just like they are my kids or something.<br/> <br/>And Yes Deb, I like the birds as well, its the cherry on top for me.  I dont know if they were sleeping or not but thats my best assumption.  I would like to come back to this town, it was a lot of fun.</td>', 'Originally posted by ccarter: Nice shot deserving of the award - but expected more then a yellow? A bit arrogant I''d say.   Like Levt said, hoping is a better word.  If you dont shoot for the best and have high expectations for your work then your work will not improve as quickly.  I want to be the best and so I shoot like it, and that mentality has done me well in my professional career. This is literally my favorite picture that I have taken so far, I only want the best for it, I take a lot of pride in them, just like they are my kids or something. And Yes Deb, I like the birds as well, its the cherry on top for me.  I dont know if they were sleeping or not but thats my best assumption.  I would like to come back to this town, it was a lot of fun.', '2011-06-30 16:56:20.000000', NULL, 0),
